/packs/
/.vscode/
/.claude/
# The specs and findings are local-only working documents: they were removed
# from git history on 2026-07-26 (public repo — see CLAUDE.md's store-visibility
# reasoning for why internal planning does not get published). They still exist
# on disk and remain mandatory pre-reading (CLAUDE.md, backend/CLAUDE.md,
# delta_test.go all cite docs/); they are simply not tracked. Nothing under
# /docs/ is re-included — a partial exception is what made the previous
# commented-out /docs/* + !DELTA-TAIL-SPEC.md dance necessary.
/docs/
/FINDINGS-PLAN.md
/.wrangler/

# Frontend
/frontend/node_modules/
/frontend/.parcel-cache/
/frontend/dist/
/dist/

# The admin console is a Parcel bundle built into backend/webui/dist by
# `make build-admin`. It is generated (like /dist), except for the committed
# placeholder index.html that keeps `go build`/`go vet`/`go test` compiling the
# //go:embed without Node. A local build overwrites the placeholder; restore it
# with `git checkout backend/webui/dist/index.html` before committing.
/backend/webui/dist/*
!/backend/webui/dist/index.html

# design-sync build output (regenerable; see .design-sync/NOTES.md)
/ds-bundle/

# SRR Cloud worker (cloud/worker): the staged shell bundle is generated by
# `make build-cloud` from dist/srrf; wrangler state, the real dev secrets and
# the real deployment config never belong in git — this repo is public, and
# wrangler.toml carries one operator's hostname, zone and login URL while
# .dev.vars carries the session secret and the tenant roster (personal data).
# Both have committed templates: wrangler.example.toml and .dev.vars.example,
# and `make` materializes wrangler.toml from its example when absent.
/cloud/worker/public/
/cloud/worker/node_modules/
/cloud/worker/.wrangler/
/cloud/worker/.dev.vars
/cloud/worker/wrangler.toml
